- Upstream (public): https://github.com/ryanbr/noop
  Pinned for these docs at 2a1de7609843b095505274ad6fc811757210be80.
  License file: https://github.com/ryanbr/noop/blob/2a1de7609843b095505274ad6fc811757210be80/LICENSE
  Confirmed in that file: PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0, Copyright 2026 NoopApp.
  The same LICENSE blob (sha b40834319bf79d0cf88ac46fb683dc21fa661cd9) is at the
  root of the private fork https://github.com/ryanhill4L/noop

- Private fork used as the lesson source: https://github.com/ryanhill4L/noop
  HEAD 0a6bad593a8966cd0d48056b40e362dcca4d040a.
  WAL durability fix: pull request 3, merge ec3032010ff177098b304394d4a37380d4661264.

NOOP's LICENSE limits itself to NOOP's original source and documentation. It
says the protocol facts in that repository are uncopyrightable facts about
bytes on a wire. Aloft's docs summarize those facts and link to the files.
A later port of NOOP source stays under PolyForm Noncommercial and must keep
this notice.

Prior research NOOP credits, and which Aloft does not copy source from
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

NOOP's NOTICE says these projects state no license, and that NOOP reimplemented
facts rather than redistributing their code. Aloft does the same. Do not paste
their source into this repo.

- johnmiddleton12/my-whoop — https://github.com/johnmiddleton12/my-whoop
  WHOOP 4.0 protocol facts.
- b-nnett/goose — https://github.com/b-nnett/goose
  WHOOP 5.0 / MG ("puffin") protocol facts.

Dependencies
------------

None yet. When the store is written, NOOP uses GRDB.swift (MIT) over SQLite.
If Aloft takes that dependency, keep GRDB's MIT license beside this notice and
do not treat the combined work as commercially licensed. ZIPFoundation (MIT)
is an upstream NOOP dependency for export import; Aloft has no import path yet.
